  "id": "vestibulospinal-tract",
  "term": "vestibulospinal tract",
  "definition": "The vestibulospinal tract is a nerve pathway that carries balance-related signals from the vestibular organs of the inner ear, through the vestibular nucleus, to the spinal cord. It works through lateral and medial pathways to help control posture, antigravity muscles, and balance during standing and walking.",
